{"repositoryId":233233797,"availability":"available","full":"linchpin/post-type-spotlight","name":"post-type-spotlight","description":"Allows admin chosen post types to have a featured post check box on the edit screen. Also adds appropriate classes to front end post display, and allows featured posts to be queried via a taxonomy query.","category":"Other","language":"PHP","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2020-01-11T13:11:35Z","updated":"2026-10-16T04:14:00Z","license":"GPL-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["linchpin","wordpress","wordpress-plugin"],"demo":"https://wordpress.org/playground/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:25.870Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:25.870Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:25.870Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T07:15:25.870Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Feature any post type — posts, pages, attachments, or your own — and then query, style and sort by that flag.","The plugin adds a Feature this post control to the editor. It only appears on the post types an administrator enables under Settings → Writing.","Because the flag is a taxonomy term rather than post meta, finding featured content is an indexed taxonomy lookup instead of a meta query. WordPress' own sticky posts only work on the core post type; this works on any type you enable."],"features":["It receives featured and featured-{$posttype} classes through the postclass filter.","A ⭐️ appears in a Featured column on that post type's admin list screen, with a Featured view that filters to just those posts.","It is assigned the hidden ptsfeaturetax taxonomy term featured, so it can be queried with a standard taxquery."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/linchpin/post-type-spotlight/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"25a35412b8d3c844753847f88ceadd9a86a348b7362579c6734fe090ed26b7ca","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:25.959Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:25.959Z"